{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'git diff --stat; git status --short; cat ANSWERS.md'","aggregated_output":"?? ANSWERS.md\n# Parcels code answers\n\n## Q1\n\nShipping is free for orders worth **€60.00 or more after discounts**, for destinations supported by the code's EU list. The destination check happens before the free-shipping check, so an unsupported destination still raises `CannotShip`. Sources: `parcels/settings.py:14-15`, `parcels/quote.py:25-32`, `parcels/carriers.py:22-24`.\n\nTo change the threshold without editing code, set the `PARCELS_FREE_FROM` environment variable before starting the process, for example `PARCELS_FREE_FROM=75.00 python -m parcels 75.00 3.2 DE`. Settings are read once at import, so changing the environment of an already running process does not refresh the threshold. Sources: `parcels/settings.py:1-15`, `parcels/__main__.py:1`.\n\n## Q2\n\nAn order heavier than the **31.5 kg** parcel limit is split into the smallest possible number of parcels: the total weight divided by 31.5, rounded up to a whole parcel count. All parcels receive the same calculated weight, rounded up to the nearest gram. For example, 70 kg becomes three parcels of 23.334 kg each. Sources: `parcels/settings.py:17`, `parcels/packing.py:11-22`.\n\nFor paid shipping, the cost is the sum of the individual parcel prices. Each parcel incurs the carrier's base price plus a charge per started kilogram, and a surcharge when the destination is outside the Netherlands. Orders meeting the free-shipping threshold return zero before packing or pricing. Sources: `parcels/quote.py:17-22`, `parcels/quote.py:31-33`.\n\n## Q3\n\nThe default carrier is **PostNL** (`postnl`). Set `PARCELS_CARRIER` before starting the process to choose `dhl`, `ups`, or `postnl`, for example `PARCELS_CARRIER=ups python -m parcels 45.00 3.2 DE`. The value is converted to lowercase; an unrecognized value raises `RuntimeError` at import. Settings are read once at import. Sources: `parcels/settings.py:1-12`.\n\nThe chosen carrier selects the tariff used to price every parcel. Sources: `parcels/quote.py:17-21`, `parcels/carriers.py:16-20`.\n\n## Q4\n\nA Friday order at **17:00** is after the **15:00 cutoff** (orders exactly at 15:00 also count as late), so the calculation first moves its start date forward by one calendar day to Saturday. It then adds **one handling day plus the destination's transit days**, counting only weekdays after that start date. Sources: `parcels/delivery.py:11`, `parcels/delivery.py:25-30`, `parcels/settings.py:18`, `parcels/delivery.py:14-22`.\n\nThe resulting delivery day depends on the destination:\n\n| Destination | Transit days | Total working days added | Delivery for Friday at 17:00 |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Netherlands (`NL`) | 1 | 2 | Following Tuesday |\n| Belgium, Germany, Luxembourg (`BE`, `DE`, `LU`) | 2 | 3 | Following Wednesday |\n| Other supported destinations | 4 | 5 | Following Friday |\n\nSources: `parcels/delivery.py:9-10`, `parcels/delivery.py:25-30`, `parcels/settings.py:18`.\n\n**Weekends are skipped; public holidays are not.** The working-day loop checks only whether the weekday is Monday through Friday, so a public holiday on a weekday counts as a working day. Source: `parcels/delivery.py:14-22`.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
